!type: Basic Math

!id: MFZGG2uCEf
!front: State the completeness (least upper bound) axiom of \( \mathbb{R} \).
!back:
If \( A \subseteq \mathbb{R} \) is:

- nonempty, and
- bounded above,

then \( A \) has a least upper bound \( \sup A \in \mathbb{R} \).
~~~

!type: Cloze Math

!id: 8GSbuJDsu0
!text: The {{c2::completeness axiom::axiom name}} is also know as the {{c1::least upper bound axiom::axiom name}} of \( \mathbb{R} \).
~~~
